{"nodes": [{"id": "roadmap_ledger_vs_tracker", "label": "Ledger vs tracker distinction", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "ROADMAP.md", "source_location": "L14-16", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "What exists today is a ledger. A ledger tells you what happened; a tracker tells you whether it's going the way you meant. Most of the roadmap is the distance between the two."}, {"id": "roadmap_categories_screen", "label": "Categories management screen (missing)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "ROADMAP.md", "source_location": "L17-24, L93", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "saveCategory and removeCategory exist in store.ts and are called from nowhere, so the user is locked to the seeded categories forever. Wallets got this screen and categories didn't \u2014 'a bug wearing a feature's clothes', and mostly a copy of Wallets.tsx."}, {"id": "roadmap_search_date_range", "label": "Search and date range filter", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "ROADMAP.md", "source_location": "L29-33", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "There is currently no way to find a past transaction except paging Month backwards. A search over note and category name plus a from/to filter fits the existing pure-function pattern in money.ts and needs no data model change."}, {"id": "roadmap_save_confirmation", "label": "Confirmation feedback after saving", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "ROADMAP.md", "source_location": "L34-36", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The sheet closing and the row appearing is the entire feedback today; a brief highlight on the new row would close the loop."}, {"id": "roadmap_budgets", "label": "Budgets per category per month", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "ROADMAP.md", "source_location": "L40-44", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The biggest single addition and the one that fits the app's name: a cap you check yourself against, one month at a time. Month already computes categoryBreakdown \u2014 a budget is that number against a target."}, {"id": "roadmap_recurring_prompts", "label": "Recurring transactions that prompt, not auto-write", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "ROADMAP.md", "source_location": "L45-49", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A ledger that inserts rows you didn't authorise is a ledger you stop trusting, and trusting it is the whole point. Due items appear as a 'confirm these' strip on Log."}, {"id": "roadmap_trends", "label": "Trends (sparkline, per-category over time)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "ROADMAP.md", "source_location": "L50-52", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Answers 'is this getting worse', which no current screen can."}, {"id": "roadmap_csv_export", "label": "CSV export", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "ROADMAP.md", "source_location": "L53-55", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Partly a backup, partly trust \u2014 an app holding your money history should have a visible exit door. Cheap: a pure function over Txn[] plus a download."}, {"id": "roadmap_debts", "label": "Debts / utang with partial payments", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "ROADMAP.md", "source_location": "L58-63", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The tricky part is that a repayment is both a debt event and a wallet movement; double-counting it would break the totals the same way transfers would have."}, {"id": "roadmap_savings_goals", "label": "Savings goals", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "ROADMAP.md", "source_location": "L64-66", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A target amount and date against a wallet; small if it leans on walletBalances. Open design question: is a goal a property of a wallet or its own thing?"}, {"id": "roadmap_receipt_photos", "label": "Receipt photos", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "ROADMAP.md", "source_location": "L67-69", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The Instant app already has $files, so the storage exists; the cost is UI and sync weight, not backend."}, {"id": "roadmap_shared_expenses", "label": "Shared or split expenses", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "ROADMAP.md", "source_location": "L70-72, L82-85", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Breaks the architecture rather than adding to it: owner-scoped permissions allow a row only when auth.id == data.owner, and split expenses need rows visible to two accounts. That's a permissions redesign, not a feature."}, {"id": "roadmap_multi_currency", "label": "Multi-currency support", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "ROADMAP.md", "source_location": "L73-79", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "money.ts hardcodes en-PH and PHP. A second currency means a currency per wallet, a rate at time of transaction, and a decision about what a cross-currency 'total' even means. Large."}, {"id": "roadmap_generic_records_table", "label": "Generic records table (ns, recordId, item)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "ROADMAP.md", "source_location": "L74-78", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Deliberately generic so new collections need no schema push \u2014 finances:budgets, finances:recurring, finances:debts all just work under the existing prefix convention. Called out as a real advantage worth spending."}, {"id": "roadmap_owner_scoped_permissions", "label": "Owner-scoped permissions (instant.perms.ts)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "ROADMAP.md", "source_location": "L82-85", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A row is allowed only when auth.id == data.owner. Every roadmap item fits under that rule except shared expenses."}, {"id": "roadmap_category_deletion_orphans", "label": "Category deletion must not orphan references", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "ROADMAP.md", "source_location": "L86-89", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Budgets and recurring items both point at a category id. walletBalances already handles the equivalent for deleted wallets by skipping unknown ids \u2014 the same discipline applies."}, {"id": "src_store_savecategory", "label": "saveCategory", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "ROADMAP.md", "source_location": "L19-20", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "src_store_removecategory", "label": "removeCategory", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "ROADMAP.md", "source_location": "L19-20", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "roadmap_ledger_vs_tracker", "target": "roadmap_budgets", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "ROADMAP.md", "source_location": "L14-16, L40-44", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "roadmap_categories_screen", "target": "src_store_savecategory", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "ROADMAP.md", "source_location": "L19-20", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "roadmap_categories_screen", "target": "src_store_removecategory", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "ROADMAP.md", "source_location": "L19-20", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "roadmap_categories_scr